<title>SINGAPORE: Maintenance of Dai Hung oil field delayed to Aug.</title>
<headline>Maintenance of Dai Hung oil field delayed to Aug.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>A maintenance shut down at Vietnam's 10,000 barrels-per-day (bpd) Dai Hung oil field has been delayed to August from the end of June, an industry source said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The source declined to explain the delay or give any other details.</p>
<p>A separate source familiar with the field said the shut down was likely to last around five weeks, in line with the original schedule.</p>
<p>The equity producers of Dai Hung are Malaysia's state-owned Petronas with 20 percent, Japan's Sumitomo with 10.625 percent, state-owned PetroVietnam with 15 percent and France's Total SA with 10.625 percent.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3571)</p>
